    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1938162820740506055",
      "url": "https://x.com/gmanews/status/1938162820740506055",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/gmanews/status/1938162820740506055",
      "text": "Tension broke out between protesters and police officers on Thursday morning during a rally for LGTBQ+ rights along Recto Avenue in Manila.  The protesters were initially blocked by a yellow barricade set up by the Manila Police District as they marched to Mendiola Bridge.\n\nThe protesters are campaigning for the passage of the SOGIE Equality Bill, as well as other issues affecting the LGBTQ+ community, during the country's celebration of Pride Month.\n\nBecause of the protest action, authorities closed both lanes of Recto Avenue between Loyola Street and Mendiola in front of the University of the East, Super Radyo dzBB's Manny Vargas reported.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/Y6aOREnSTv",
